{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Do not turn to their meal-offering.</b> The reason Moses cursed Dathan and Abiram is that when Moses sent to call them, they said 'we will not go up.' Their intention was not to repent — even if HaShem were to say 'I have chosen Aaron,' they would still contest the priesthood. But Korah and the two hundred and fifty men who took it upon themselves, each taking his firepan — they thought that HaShem had not sent Aaron his brother, but that he did it on his own. He did not wish to curse them. 'Nor have I taken one donkey from them' is turned about to mean: why do you exalt yourselves?" "<b>One donkey.</b> According to the vocalization (nequd), the meaning is as it sounds. But according to Rashi, it should have been vocalized as אחד העם, 'one of the people.'" "<b>I have taken.</b> An expression of taking, like ישאו דבלת תאנים, 'they shall carry cakes of figs,' and וישאם דוד ואנשיו, 'and David and his men carried them.'" "<b>Nor have I done harm to any one of them.</b> Even though they informed against me concerning the killing of the Egyptian."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:17.729715296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}